Week 1 Mini Project: Linux Server Health Check
Project Goal

Create a script that:

✅ Displays the hostname
✅ Displays uptime
✅ Shows CPU usage
✅ Shows memory usage
✅ Shows disk usage
✅ Checks whether Jenkins is running
✅ Saves the report with a timestamp
✅ Returns exit code 0 if all checks pass, or a non-zero exit code if Jenkins is not running
Step 1: Create a Project Directory
mkdir ~/mini-project
cd ~/mini-project

Verify:

pwd

Example output:

/home/ec2-user/mini-project
Step 2: Create the Script
touch health-check.sh

Verify:

ls -l
Step 3: Edit the Script

Open it with your preferred editor:

vi health-check.sh

Paste the following script:

#!/bin/bash

# Log file name with timestamp
LOGFILE="health_report_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S).log"

echo "==========================================" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
echo " Linux Server Health Check Report" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
echo "==========================================" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo "Date: $(date)" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Hostname:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
hostname | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Uptime:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
uptime | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "CPU Load:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
uptime | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Memory Usage:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
free -h | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Disk Usage:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
df -h | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Checking Jenkins Service..." | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

if systemctl is-active --quiet jenkins
then
    echo "Jenkins Service: RUNNING" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
    EXIT_CODE=0
else
    echo "Jenkins Service: NOT RUNNING" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
    EXIT_CODE=1
fi

echo ""
echo "Top 5 CPU Processes:" | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
ps -eo pid,comm,%cpu --sort=-%cpu | head -6 | tee -a "$LOGFILE"

echo ""
echo "Health check completed." | tee -a "$LOGFILE"
echo "Report saved to: $LOGFILE"

exit $EXIT_CODE
Step 4: Make the Script Executable
chmod +x health-check.sh

Verify:

